        "finalText": "RCSB PDB's search service returns **10 entries** with a protein entity mapped to human leptin.\n\n1. **Accession:** UniProtKB's search gives one reviewed (Swiss-Prot) entry for human gene LEP: **P41159** (Leptin, also called \"Obese protein\").\n2. **Search endpoint:** The RCSB Search provider that was already loaded points at the retired `/rcsbsearch/v1` path. Every call to it returned HTTP 404, including a plain full-text search. I had RightClick X learn the current spec from `https://search.rcsb.org/openapi.json` and ran the query there.\n3. **Query:** I searched for entries where `rcsb_polymer_entity_container_identifiers.reference_sequence_identifiers.database_accession` exactly matches `P41159`, with `database_name` set to `UniProt`. I asked for all hits.\n\nThe result reported `total_count: 10`:\n1AX8, 7Z3Q, 8AVE, 8AVF, 8AVO, 8K6Z, 8X80, 8X81, 8X85, 9PUO\n\nThis is a live result and the count will change as RCSB adds new structures.\n\nANSWER: 10 | 1AX8, 7Z3Q, 8AVE, 8AVF, 8AVO, 8K6Z, 8X80, 8X81, 8X85, 9PUO"
